 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "Bracket the sentence first. 'Unless Z' qualifies the whole promise 'if X then Y'.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l1",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "'A unless Z' means 'if not Z, then A'. With A = (X → Y) this is ¬Z → (X → Y).",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Exportation moves the outer hypothesis inside: A → (B → C) ≡ (A ∧ B) → C. The result is (X ∧ ¬Z) → Y.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Check with the forbidden situation. The sentence is broken only if X happens, Z does not, and Y fails: X = T, Y = F, Z = F. The formula is false on exactly that row.",
